      "text": "To solve the expression \\(1 + 6 \\cdot 2 - 3 + 5 \\cdot 4 \\div 2\\), we need to follow the order of operations, often remembered by the acronym PEMDAS (Parentheses, Exponents, Multiplication and Division (from left to right), Addition and Subtraction (from left to right)).\n\nFirst, we perform the multiplication and division from left to right:\n1. \\(6 \\cdot 2 = 12\\)\n2. \\(5 \\cdot 4 \\div 2 = 5 \\cdot 4 = 20 \\div 2 = 10\\)\n\nNow the expression simplifies to:\n\\[1 + 12 - 3 + 10\\]\n\nNext, we perform the addition and subtraction from left to right:\n1. \\(1 + 12 = 13\\)\n2. \\(13 - 3 = 10\\)\n3. \\(10 + 10 = 20\\)\n\nSo the final answer is \\(20\\). We can confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Compute the expression step by step\nexpression_result = 1 + 6 * 2 - 3 + 5 * 4 / 2\nprint(expression_result)\n```\n```output\n20.0\n```\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{20}\\).",
