    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the expression \\(1 + 6 \\cdot 2 - 3 + 5 \\cdot 4 \\div 2\\) step by step, we need to follow the order of operations, also known as BODMAS (Brackets, Orders, Division and Multiplication, Addition and Subtraction).\n\n1. **Division and Multiplication**: According to BODMAS, we perform the division and multiplication operations from left to right.\n\n   - First, perform the multiplication \\(6 \\cdot 2\\) and \\(5 \\cdot 4\\):\n     \\[\n     6 \\cdot 2 = 12\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     5 \\cdot 4 = 20\n     \\]\n   - Then, perform the division \\(20 \\div 2\\):\n     \\[\n     20 \\div 2 = 10\n     \\]\n\n2. **Substitution and Simplification**: After performing the division and multiplication, substitute these values back into the expression:\n   \\[\n   1 + 12 - 3 + 10\n   \\]\n\n3. **Arithmetic Operations**: We now perform the addition and subtraction from left to right:\n   - First, perform the addition \\(1 + 12\\):\n     \\[\n     1 + 12 = 13\n     \\]\n   - Then, perform the subtraction \\(13 - 3\\):\n     \\[\n     13 - 3 = 10\n     \\]\n   - Finally, perform the last addition \\(10 + 10\\):\n     \\[\n     10 + 10 = 20\n     \\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{20}\n\\]",
